Message-ID: <CAG2Vd7ie=PJA_4cLfvQThX6ui14sm8k-NHxhnho4KFAg3jAr9g@mail.gmail.com>

Dear Zhenguang,

sum coding differs from treatment/dummy coding (which is what I assume you
mean by simple coding) in that there is no reference level. The difference
becomes most apparent when you have an interaction of A and B in your
model. Even in a balanced data set, treatment coding results in
collinearity between the interaction and its main effects, whereas sum
coding does not (looking at
http://hlplab.files.wordpress.com/2011/02/codingtutorial.pdf might help).

Can you post the output of the sum coded model? Also, make sure to not
subset the data frame after applying contr. commands as this can undo those
commands.

Florian


