>>>>         here. I read in
>>>>         somewhere that the A2 line could be interpreted as the main
>>>>         effect of
>>>>         the A factor, the B2 line as the main effect of the B
>>>>         factor, and the
>>>>         A2:B2 as the interaction (e.g., Tables 5 and 7 in Jaeger,
>>>>         2008, if I
>>>>         have understood his interpretation of them correctly).
