From: iva.m.ivanova-Re5JQEeQqe8AvxtiuMwx3w at public.gmane.org (Iva Ivanova)
Date: Mon, 21 Jan 2013 12:07:39 -0800
Subject: queries regarding significance of interaction term, simple effects, and false convergence
Message-ID: <CAE3_nMSSKZ8LbBN8G7L7MuZf4eh0==pvkqTR=ahdgN4nsKWEaA@mail.gmail.com>

Hi!

I am analyzing several 2 x 2 syntactic priming experiments with logit mixed
effects models, and I have several questions.

1) My first question concerns the presence or absence of interaction in
Exp. 1. When I use the maximal random effects structure as recommended by
Barr et al. -
exp1.full<- lmer(data ~ A*B
+(1+A*B|subj)+(1+A*B|item),data=exp1,family=binomial)
the interaction term is not significant. However, I had previously analyzed
these results with ANOVA, and the interaction was significant. Also, when I
use a simplified model:
exp1.1<- lmer(data ~ A*B +(1+A+B|subj)+(1|item),data=exp1,family=binomial)
the interaction is also significant.
