> 2) My second question concerns what is the best way to get at simple main
> effects. That is, I would like to know whether A1 is significantly
> different from A2 for each level of B. Is it all right to fit a separate
> model only on the data from B1, and then only on the data from B2?
>

You can do that, but that will not be a simple effect. I.e., you will lose
power. To run a simple effect equivalent, simply remove the main effect
from the model

data ~ A + A:B + (1 + A + A:B  | subj) + (1 + A + A:B | item)

should give you the main effect of A, and two simple effects for B at the
different levels of A.


