lol, looks like Scott just answered my email the very second I sent mine!
And to quote him

"Your exp2 data is even more "defective", however, when you look at
things by subject: it looks like you have 17 people who responded "0"
to everything, and 7 who responded "1" to everything!"

So, yes, that's the reason why the models don't converge. You might read
Jaeger et al (2012-Linguistic Typology) for a discussion of exactly that
problem (in that case applied to typological analyses) and simulations that
explore the problem further:
http://www.academia.edu/753571/Jaeger_T._F._Graff_P._Croft_B._and_Pontillo_D._2011._Mixed_effect_models_for_genetic_and_areal_dependencies_in_linguistic_typology_Commentary_on_Atkinson._Linguistic_Typology_15_2_281-319

Florian


On Mon, Jan 21, 2013 at 10:21 PM, T. Florian Jaeger <tiflo-sMaJTQEtWn7RrdkEUGVx5Q at public.gmane.orgu
> wrote:

